// Package observability provides structured logging, OTel tracing, Prometheus
// metrics, and the canonical error envelope used by every OmniCore service.
//
// Logger: log/slog with OTel-trace-context bridge. Reads x-request-id,
// x-trace-id, x-tenant-id, x-user-id from context.Context and emits them
// as structured fields on every log line.
//
// Tracer: thin wrapper over go.opentelemetry.io/otel. SetupTracer is called
// once at service start; Tracer() returns the global named tracer.
//
// Meter (Path B / direct Prometheus scrape, Admin Phase 5 §3):
//
//	SetupMeter(ctx, "my-svc", version) — call once at service start.
//	  Initialises a per-process prometheus.Registry, registers Go runtime +
//	  process collectors, registers a service_up{version="..."} gauge (constant 1),
//	  and stores a process-wide OTel MeterProvider backed by the Prometheus
//	  exporter. Returns a shutdown/flush func the caller MUST defer.
//
//	MetricsHandler() — returns an http.Handler serving Prometheus text format.
//	  Mount at /metrics on a sidecar HTTP listener (gRPC services) or the
//	  existing chi router (BFFs).
//
//	UnaryServerMetricsInterceptor() / StreamServerMetricsInterceptor() — gRPC
//	  server interceptors that record omnicore_request_duration_seconds,
//	  omnicore_requests_total, and omnicore_requests_in_flight.
//
//	HTTPMetricsMiddleware() — chi-compatible http.Handler middleware recording
//	  the same three instruments. Route label is chi's RoutePattern (bounded
//	  cardinality); status_class is 2xx/4xx/5xx.
//
//	GlobalMeterProvider() — returns the OTel MeterProvider for services that
//	  need custom instruments beyond the generic request set.
//
// Error: structured error envelope with a fixed ErrorCode enum, a human
// message, the originating request_id, and an optional cause. gRPC servers
// translate Error to an appropriate google.rpc.Code; REST handlers translate
// it to an HTTP status. MFEs map the code to user-facing toast text and
// never display raw messages.
package observability


