// test for F21 / issue #1827: a chi router mounted at the root (as shell-bff
// does, pre-auth) must never let an unauthenticated caller mint a new
// Prometheus label set by hitting an arbitrary nonexistent path. When chi's
// RouteContext exists but RoutePattern() is empty (no route matched — the
// 404 path), the middleware must emit the fixed "unmatched" sentinel instead
